==Strategy==
After No Return Flights got demolished on every difficulty via anti-Traitless powercreep, it went to Hell and got Relic and Dark enemies. While you might assume that you can just spam UL Mythics to beat the stage, it isn't nearly as straightforward as that.

This stage starts off without too much, although you need to take caution to not hit the base prematurely. The best way to do so is to kill the last enemy on screen with [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]], then stall for cash and until Doron is off cooldown.

When you hit the base, you are greeted with M. Ost, Dark enemies, and Shachiko. Shachiko's appearance should not be underestimated: while normally you just send out [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] to destroy it, in this stage killing M. Ost is a higher priority, meaning you'll have to deal with Shachiko throughout the whole stage. Lure M. Ost to your base, and do your best to murder him fast with Doron, Idi, either [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] or [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Nova]] and supplemental damage from [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. Once M. Ost goes down, you still can't relax much given that the combination of Shachiko, Dark Otters and Darkmadillos can still serve as a genuine threat. Because anti-Dark options like Pizza are a nightmare to get through with Shachiko sniping everything, your best method to kill the Dark supporting enemies is with pure brute force options like generalist Esoteric Uril/Nova, Slapsticks, and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]]. Alongside hits from [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] to get chip damage onto the Miz Devils and Darkmadillos, as long as you meatshield well and constantly apply pressure onto Shachiko, it and Le'noir should fall after a while, and once they do you have free reign to beat the base up and win.

